      "documentConcept": "Epidemiology and environmental risk factors: paraquat, TCE, air pollution",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:7fdaf40c97497c65bb9f74ff0a3f40d9b9404b8420445f187a6eaab2cf46eae0",
      "text": "PD epidemiology includes a rising global burden (Global Burden of Disease estimates and projections) and potentially modifiable environmental exposures. Observational studies associate paraquat, TCE-containing solvent exposures and some air pollutants with PD, but estimates and causal interpretations vary. Paraquat findings include positive case-control results, null workforce mortality evidence and a qualified EPA assessment finding no clear link for labeled uses. TCE evidence includes a small twin study and the mixed-exposure Camp Lejeune cohort. Air-pollution evidence includes positive pooled and Taiwanese results alongside an adjusted overall null Northern Ireland result. Forecasts, odds ratios, exposure mixtures and study outcomes require separate interpretation.",
      "sources": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10041423/",
